    {
      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_96946b5d",
      "@type": "OverallIntent",
      "instance_name": "overallintent_instance",
      "label": "the overallintent",
      "description": "meme-id: i_like_my_coffee_like_i_like_my_slaves_extra_dark; hasOverallIntent: Hateful; overall-intent-description: The meme juxtaposes a serious, authoritative image of a man (likely a historical or political figure) with the text 'I like my coffee like I like my slaves' and 'extra dark'. This creates a hateful analogy that equates the preference for dark coffee with the ownership of human beings, which is a direct and offensive reference to slavery. The intent is to provoke shock or humor by invoking a deeply harmful historical and moral atrocity, thereby targeting and dehumanizing enslaved people and perpetuating racist stereotypes. The visual of the man, often associated with power and authority, reinforces the hateful message by implying that such a preference is a reflection of a morally reprehensible worldview. This meme is explicitly hateful as it directly attacks a protected characteristic (race) by invoking the historical trauma of slavery.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
        "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#analysis_6c7cc473"
      },
      "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface"
    },
